The Role-based Access Control (RBAC) system operates in a multi-user environment and manages user access to resources based on roles. It supports role hierarchy, temporary role delegation, revocation of delegated roles, and concurrent request processing. The system ensures authorization correctness, consistency in delegation and permissions, liveness in request processing, and safety under concurrency. Users are assigned security clearances of High, Medium, or Low, which dictate their access levels and ability to delegate roles or approve requests. The system processes requests in FIFO order but allows for exceptions under certain conditions, such as emergency situations.

PROSPECTIVE FUNCTIONAL REQUIREMENTS
=======================
R1: Triggering Emergency Mode
